All 32 tests pass. Here's a summary of the fix:

## Root cause

The `PreferHeredocForMultiLineDoc` rule's `fix_patches/2` used `RuleHelpers.patches_from_postwalk`, which diffs ASTs structurally via `diff_patches`. That function compares only the `form` and `args` of 3-tuples — it **ignores the metadata** (middle element). When the fix only changed the `:delimiter` key in the string block's metadata (the `real_multi_line?` path where the value already ends with `\n`), the diff saw no divergence and returned `[]`.

This showed up in production when `NoDuplicateFunctionClauses` converted a heredoc to a regular multi-line string, then `PreferHeredocForMultiLineDoc` detected the issue but couldn't fix it.

## Fix

Changed `fix_patches/2` from `patches_from_postwalk` to a whole-source rendering approach:

1. `Macro.postwalk(ast, &fix_doc_node/1)` transforms the AST (same as before)
2. `Sourceror.to_string(transformed)` renders the fixed AST
3. A single whole-source patch replaces the entire source with the rendered output

This avoids both problems:
- **Metadata-only changes**: `transformed == ast` uses deep equality (includes metadata), so changes are detected
- **Sourceror.patch_string newline swallowing**: the whole-source patch doesn't have a multi-line range issue

## Regression test added

Added `"converts real-newline @doc (not escaped \\n) to heredoc"` to the fix test — exercises the `real_multi_line?` path where the string value contains actual newlines (not `\n` escapes).[0m
